<!-- PORTED from ConditioningControlPanel/Windows/EmiDesk/EmiRingWindow.xaml.
     Every property preserved; the deviations below are all forced.

       WindowStyle="None" + AllowsTransparency="True"  -> SystemDecorations="None" +
                                                          TransparencyLevelHint="Transparent"
       ResizeMode="NoResize"                           -> CanResize="False"
       SizeToContent="Manual"                          -> dropped; Manual IS Avalonia's default
       WindowStartupLocation="Manual"                  -> dropped; the code sets Position, and
                                                          Manual is Avalonia's default too
       SnapsToDevicePixels="True"                      -> dropped; Avalonia has UseLayoutRounding
                                                          only, which is kept
       WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW | WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, set from   -> ShowInTaskbar="False" +
       the code-behind on SourceInitialized               ShowActivated="False", declared here
       SetWindowPos(HWND_TOPMOST)                      -> Topmost="True" (Avalonia maps it to
                                                          _NET_WM_STATE_ABOVE on X11)

     The Canvas keeps NO Background, which is the one place "{x:Null} becomes Transparent" would be
     wrong: null means not hit-testable in Avalonia exactly as it does in WPF, and the comment
     below is entirely about the gaps in the fan staying clickable.

     The 600x400 size is the WPF original's; Layout() replaces it with the fan's own bounding box
     before the window is ever shown. -->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="ConditioningControlPanel.Avalonia.Views.Windows.EmiDesk.EmiRingWindow"
        Title="EMI ring"

        SystemDecorations="None"
        TransparencyLevelHint="Transparent"
        Background="Transparent"
        ShowActivated="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        CanResize="False"
        UseLayoutRounding="True"
        Topmost="True"
        Focusable="False"
        Width="600" Height="400">

    <!--
        THE RING.

        NO IsVisible="False" HERE (the book's lesson - see EmiBookWindow.xaml). This window is
        built by EnsureRing and shown by OpenRing in the SAME dispatcher turn, so a XAML hide is
        queued against a window that does not exist yet and lands after Show: the window goes
        invisible while IsOpen and IsVisible keep reading true. That was the whole of "I gotta
        click 2 or 3 times for the wheel to pop up" - the first open was real but invisible, and
        the next click went to the global close hook and folded it. A Window is not visible until
        Show() runs anyway, so the property simply goes.

        A SIBLING window, not a layer inside EmiDeskWindow: the widget carries only 120 DIPs of pad
        around her silhouette, and a full fan at a 420 DIP body needs far more than that. This
        window is sized to the WORK AREA of the monitor she is standing on, so a card can be
        clamped anywhere on that screen without a second resize, and it is parked with the same
        physical-pixels-over-DPI arithmetic the widget uses (SEAMS.md: BodyScreenRect and
        RingAnchorScreenPoint are PHYSICAL PIXELS, never DIPs).

        Nothing in here is hit-testable except the cards themselves - on Windows, where a layered
        window does not hit-test fully transparent pixels. On X11 a window hit-tests its whole
        rectangle whatever its alpha, so the gaps in the fan are NOT click-through on this head
        yet; see the ponytail note about X11Overlay in the code-behind.
    -->
    <Canvas x:Name="Field" ClipToBounds="False"/>
</Window>
